r the rollback the service reports healthy with a 0.2% error rate. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 17151, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013QQczcnJjuRzatKKaxWsLa", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 17151, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013QQczcnJjuRzatKKaxWsLa", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 21172, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 and opened a SEV2 incident. The service is healthy again in all regions.\n\n- **What was wrong:** The latest release, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with 18% of requests returning errors. The release candidate before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also marked unhealthy, so the most recent healthy release was v2.3.0.\n- **Rollback:** All three regions are now on v2.3.0. A fresh status check shows the service healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged the on-call engineer. It says what failed, that we rolled back and how the service looks now. It also says to find out why v2.3.1 broke before redeploying it. There were no open incidents before this one.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0183LCcnLV1HBCN8kHHUHFt3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WDbwseX2RESEWYkapWRmbu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01875wuRsmk9nRQ2e9LciLWJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01D3gWPatbUx3sBidHDd9Cn8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DmwdeztnwUPnFKUHo9wr7v", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013QQczcnJjuRzatKKaxWsLa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the latest deploy of v2.3.1 (unhealthy in all regions, error rate 18%). The previous candidate v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). After the rollback the service reports healthy with a 0.2% error rate. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 and opened a SEV2 incident. The service is healthy again in all regions.\n\n- **What was wrong:** The latest release, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with 18% of requests returning errors. The release candidate before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also marked unhealthy, so the most recent healthy release was v2.3.0.\n- **Rollback:** All three regions are now on v2.3.0. A fresh status check shows the service healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged the on-call engineer. It says what failed, that we rolled back and how the service looks now. It also says to find out why v2.3.1 broke before redeploying it. There were no open incidents before this one.", "type": "text"}]}]}